        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 792,
        "paragraph_id": "14E2A446",
        "text": "The bed slope will change the threshold conditions for initiation of motion."
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 32090,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 886,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 794,
        "paragraph_id": "478C3159",
        "text": "Two possible expressions are implemented to change the magnitude of the sediment transport resulting from bed slope effects. The first method is the default one in XBeach:"
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 32220,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 890,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 798,
        "paragraph_id": "1DCBDE7F",
        "text": "Where qx and qy are calculated in equation (2.110), where α is 1.6 (keyword facsl). This method could be applied on either the total sediment transport (keyword: bdslpeffmag = roelvink_total) or only on the bed load transport (keyword: bdslpeffmag = roelvink_bed). The second method is based on the engineering formula of Soulsby (1997):"
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 32279,
